{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Like a House on Fire", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Always Together", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 18, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": " The Future Continuous and Future Perfect Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"underline\">Future Continuous </span> tense to talk about something that will be in progress at a specific time in the future. <br> When you use the <span class=\"underline\">Future Continuous</span>, the action will have begun before that moment but it will not have finished yet.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">will be sleeping</span> at 8:00 p.m. tonight. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The person will start sleeping at some point in the future and be sleeping at 8 p.m. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"underline\">Future Perfect</span> tense to talk about a future action or event that will already be completed by a certain time in the future. You use the <span class=\"underline\">Future Perfect</span>, to show the time relationship between two future events or actions. You can use <span class=\"italic\"> already</span> and <span class=\"italic\">yet</span> to emphasize which event will happen first.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">You can pick me up at 5:00 p.m. I <span class=\"strong\">will have already finished</span> my work by the time you arrive.</span> <br><span class=\"italic\">Please don't call me before 8:00 a.m. I <span class=\"strong\">won't have woken up yet!</span></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart for the structure of the Future Continuous and Future Perfect tenses:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"will (not) + be + v-ing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">At this time, next month we <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will be laughing</span> and giggling like we are 12-year-old girls again. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" will + have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Next week <span class=\\\"strong\\\">we will have been</span> friends for over 25 years.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "In fact, she told me that next week we will have been friends for over 25 years.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "At this time next month we will be laughing and giggling like we are 12-year-old girls again. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "At 10:30, Sally will be finishing up her chores.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Hopefully by then we will have gotten two more people to be on our team.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Future", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use four different tenses to talk about the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you talk about things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you ask about intentions, you use <span class=\"italic\">be going to</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future, you use the Present Continuous tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you talk about schedules, you use the Simple Present. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">What will you do on Sunday?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Be going to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We are going to have so much fun together!\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> We are getting together next month.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">The event kicks off at 1 p.m. sharp.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to look forward to", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to feel excited about something that is going to happen in the future", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We are getting together next month. I'm really looking forward to it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear when describing a friendship.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "tight knit", "type": "name"}, {"content": "emotionally close", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Are you guys still really tight knit?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "milestone", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an important event in the progress of something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What a cool milestone.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to reveal ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make something or somebody known", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We're going to reveal the mystery partners next week.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "lumberjack", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person whose job is to cut down trees for wood", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: John works in the forest as a lumberjack.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to head over", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to move toward a specific destination", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We can head over to the event from there.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Brainstorm with a group all the qualities that make a good friend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Then make a list of negative characteristics that people have.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Individually, draw a large circle.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Put three names in the circle and write one name outside the circle.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The three names inside are friends. Write 4 to 5 characteristics or qualities that keep them in your circle.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For the person outside of the circle write negative qualities or characteristics that they possess that keep them outside your circle.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share with a partner and ask questions.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I brainstorm vocabulary to help describe people.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I analyze friendships and reflect on why I am friends with certain people and not with others.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my thoughts and feelings with a partner about qualities and characteristics.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn9le18ob03re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn9le18ob03re2img01.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class= \"strong\"> Peter</span>: Ok Vanessa. Who was your best friend when you were growing up?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Vanessa</span>: Honestly, I got along best with my cousin Cindy. We were very close. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Peter</span>: Are you guys still really tight knit? <br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I talk to her once a week, either by phone or on social media. In fact, she told me that next week we will have been friends for over 25 years.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Sally</span>: That is adorable. What a cool milestone.<br />"}, {"image": "engenn9le18ob03re2img02.jpg", "time": "26000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class= \"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yeah, we're getting together next month. I'm really looking forward to it. At this time next month we will be laughing and giggling like we are 12-year-old girls again. We are going to have so much fun together!<br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Sally</span>: Quiet Peter!<br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Peter</span>: I didn't say anything!<br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Sally</span>: You were about to. It was a preemptive strike.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Peter</span>: Nice. So V. What will you do on Sunday?<br />"}, {"image": "engenn9le18ob03re2img05.jpg", "time": "51000", "id": 3, "text": "<span class= \"strong\">Vanessa</span> : Well, the event kicks off at 1:00 p.m sharp so we will need to get there a little early. At 10:30, Sally will be finishing up her chores, so you guys should come by the restaurant for brunch and then we can head over to the event from there.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Sally</span>: That sounds perfect.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  Hopefully by then we will have gotten two more people to be on our team.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Sally</span>: Right. The mystery partners have yet to be revealed.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Any suggestions?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Peter</span>: How about lumberjacks? What? I hear they're ok!<br />"}], "audiosrc": "engenn9le18ob03re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn9le18ob03re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I talk about friendship, emotions and behavior.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about future action.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about what I will be doing or what I will have done.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What qualities does a best friend have?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What sort of things cause friends to have a falling out?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]